- "any character" or an alternative inside a quantified group — `(.*a){12}`, `(\w+\.)+`;
- ladders of adjacent quantifiers with overlapping classes — `a*a*a*b`, `\d+\d+\d+$`;
- quantified backreferences, patterns that are too long (more than 1000 characters) and too deeply nested (more than 5 levels).

